WEBVTT

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:32.678
So what is included
in our cultural perception of physics?

00:03:32.702 --> 00:03:35.512
Because I'm a physicist,
there has to be a graph, right?

00:03:35.536 --> 00:03:36.692
That's allowed.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:40.977
We've got time along the bottom here,
from very fast things there,

00:03:41.001 --> 00:03:44.442
to things that take a long time over here.

00:03:44.466 --> 00:03:46.961
Small things at the bottom,
big things up there.

00:03:46.985 --> 00:03:50.010
So, our current cultural image
of physics looks like this.

00:03:50.034 --> 00:03:52.555
There's quantum mechanics
down in that corner,

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:54.579
it's very small, it's very weird,

00:03:54.603 --> 00:03:56.604
it happens very quickly,

00:03:56.628 --> 00:03:59.909
and it's a long way down
in the general ...

00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:02.767
on the scale of anything that matters
for everyday life.